      {
        "id": 194119,
        "name": "NinjaMonkey",
        "username": "NinjaMonkey",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/67e7ee/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-03-29T18:03:16.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Trajector\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/48/1914_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Trajector:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I just got home and pulled out the Void Guard character cards to remind myself of their powers.</p>\n<p>If you were playing with Malpractice Medico, HOLY CRUD is \"From the Brink\" a lot of damage!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I can definately see some powerful nuke potential here. A team of Darkwatch Nightmist, Captain Cosmic, Unity, Fanatic&nbsp;and Medico would be fun to try. Nightmist leads with a 3/4 Oblivion to damage all the constructs and bots so they can actually be&nbsp;healed&nbsp;dropping a Sacrosanct Martyr loving Fanatic in the process. 10 base damage just for the 5 heroes plus 2 per construct/bot healed.</p>\n<p>Really looking forward to these 4 decks. Happy the video game is going to be releasing&nbsp;them first when Oblivaeon goes live.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:21:13.060Z",
