      {
        "id": 194123,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-03-29T19:55:18.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Arcanist Lupus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Arcanist Lupus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Broadly speaking, all incaps could be considered \"losses of control\". If the hero was in control, they wouldn't have been incapacitated.</p>\n<p>(Luminary being the exception, of course )</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I see your point and it's totally fair. But I think that theme is more pronounced for Writhe. Legacy has an incap theme of \"loss&nbsp;in death\". Tachyon's&nbsp;shown in positions she can't run from, or where she is unable to outrun&nbsp;her problems. Wrath's themes are&nbsp;price/cost&nbsp;(similar to her F6 promo).</p>\n<p>You can make arguments that all incaps are losses of control, and it's valid, but&nbsp;a lot of characters have stronger and more&nbsp;focused themes they deal with as characters&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:21:13.344Z",
